# Netlify redirect rules. This file must sit in the publish root (site/), which is
# what netlify.toml points at -- a _redirects at the repo root is never read.
#
# The Netlify-assigned subdomain serves the entire site publicly and is indexable,
# so it competes with www.hestora.net for the same content: a third hostname
# splitting traffic and creating duplicate content for Google. Clarity recorded
# real visits landing on it. Redirecting eliminates the duplicate rather than
# merely de-listing it, and folds those visits back into the main domain.
#
# The `!` (force) is required: without it Netlify serves the existing page instead
# of redirecting, because a matching file exists at that path.
#
# Deploy previews are unaffected -- they use deploy-preview-N--hestora-site.netlify.app,
# which does not match these rules.
#
# Apex -> www is handled in Netlify Domain management (www.hestora.net is the
# PRIMARY domain), not here. See the note at the top of netlify.toml.

http://hestora-site.netlify.app/*   https://www.hestora.net/:splat  301!
https://hestora-site.netlify.app/*  https://www.hestora.net/:splat  301!
